   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <fw place="top" type="letterhead"> WOMEN'S AMERICAN ORT<lb/>212 Fifth Avenue<lb/>
               <rs type="place" ref="#tillich_place_id__319">New York</rs> 10, N.Y. </fw>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1945-09-19">September 19, 1945</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>You have been good enough in the past to sponsor the Annual Donor Luncheon given by
               Women's American ORT.<note type="ea">Das Programm Organization of Rehabilitation
                  through Training (ORT) diente der ökonomischen Rehabilitation jüdischer
                  Geflüchteter und Kriegsopfer.</note> We have now undertaken a
               Guardianship-Vocational Training Plan which calls for the adoption of at least 1000
               European Jewish war orphans who will be trained in agriculture and industry, and
               partially maintained for one year.</p>
            <p>We feel sure this is a very timely project. Extending ORT service to a thousand
               orphans will help so much to save the next generation.</p>
            <p>Would you do us the honor of sponsoring this new plan?</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed>Maurice Finkelstein</signed>
               <rs type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__3295">Mrs. Maurice Finkelstein</rs>
               National President</closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
